legal: NF-S69-13 -- privacy + terms drift fixes, AS-IS strengthening, +tax, security.txt

Pre-marketplace independent review of the live legal pages found
two outdated security claims (same drift class as F008 and NF-S69-1),
plus an opportunity to strengthen user-onus / AS-IS language to
match the actual liability posture. Closes:

PRIVACY
- privacy.html section 2.1: was 'license key transmitted as URL
  query parameter (?token=...)'. Reality since v1.13.0 is POST + JSON
  body with a hashed machine ID. Updated. Removed 'plan to migrate
  to Authorization: Bearer in a future release' (already migrated --
  the replacement is POST body, not Bearer).
- privacy.html section 5.1: was 'Cloudflare observes the request URL
  including the ?token= query parameter'. Cloudflare does not see
  query-string license keys because they're now in the POST body.
  Updated.
- privacy.html section 2.1.1 (NEW): explicitly documents that VPS
  validation differs from LT (per-request Supabase customers-table
  lookup, no machine fingerprint, no per-machine activation cap;
  parity is on the post-marketplace roadmap). Mirrors the WHITEPAPER
  fix from NF-S69-1.

TERMS
- terms.html Schedule B.2: was 'License key validation operates the
  same as local-terminal-mcp -- your license key is sent to ForgeRift's
  subscription service at startup'. VPS does NOT validate at startup;
  it validates per-request. Same drift class as the WHITEPAPER fix
  shipped earlier today (NF-S69-1). Now matches reality.
- terms.html section 8.A (NEW): explicit 8-point user-acknowledgment
  block stating that ForgeRift does not control Claude or Cowork,
  that the user is responsible for what they authorize, scope they
  configure, supervision, secrets they paste, and Anthropic policy
  compliance. Survives Term updates per Section 15. Strengthens the
  AS-IS posture without limiting mandatory consumer-protection rights.
- terms.html section 6.3: trial conversion clauses rewritten with
  a prominent red-bordered warning paragraph -- explicit 'cancel
  before day 14 or your card will be charged on day 15' wording,
  no-refunds-after-trial, point-of-purchase acknowledgment via
  Stripe checkout '14-day free trial, then /month' UI.

INDEX
- index.html: small '+ tax where applicable' notation under each
  pricing card (3 cards: Individual, Bundle, Founder). Stripe Tax
  is now enabled at the Payment Link level; the disclosure matches.

SECURITY.TXT
- /.well-known/security.txt + /security.txt (per RFC 9116) added
  with mailto:security@forgerift.io plus per-repo GitHub security
  advisory URLs and 1-year Expires.
- _config.yml created to include .well-known under Jekyll (default
  Jekyll excludes dotfile directories from GitHub Pages output).

DATES
- 'Last updated' bumped from 2026-04-29 to 2026-05-04 on both
  privacy.html and terms.html.